ere were a whole heap of narrative  challenges to overcome in that first  avengers movie the film had to  successfully convey loki as a villain  big enough for all six heroes  convincingly set up tension between them  and then proved that they're a great  team after all and then amidst all that  the avengers had to pretty much redefine  the character of the hulk luckily marvel  rose to the occasion and then some  hulk's whole arc in the film from sad  sack scientist reluctant hero is  magnificent but his best moment comes  when banner finally arrives at the final  fight in new york surrounded by the  city's ruins he utters arguably his most  famous mcu line now might be a really  good time for you to get angry  that's my secret captain  [Music]  i'm always angry and then he lets loose  with a punch that shows the hulk for  what he really is raw power hulk's had  plenty of great moments since then but  not have been quite as potent as this  x2 x-men united is among the best of  fox's x-men films largely because it's a  movie that retains what everyone liked  about the first x film while upping the  ante in just about every respect it does  this not only by keeping the focus on  wolverine and rogue but also introducing  new characters with dazzling abilities  and raising the stakes on almost every  action set piece while magneto's prison  escape is a favorite scene for some fans  for others the undisputed champion of  this film happens in its opening moments  when nightcrawler breaks into the oval  office and attempts to assassinate the  president it's later revealed that  nightcrawler has been brainwashed and  that his plight is at the center of a  massive conspiracy to rid the world of  mutant kind he also turns out to be a  perfectly nice guy who'd never  deliberately do what he did in the  film's opening minutes but that doesn't  stop the sequence from packing a serious  punch and even today it remains one of  the most thrilling action scenes in the  world of comic book movies since its  release in 2004 spider-man 2 has been  followed by six other spider-man films  four of which starred other actors as  the iconic web slinger but for many fans  sam raimi's sequel remains a gold  standard for both spidey and superhero  movies largely thanks to its emotional  core and superb action sequences this is  best demonstrated in the still legendary  sequence in which spider-man has to stop  a runaway train after dr octopus  sabotages the controls though it would  later be topped in scope by homecoming's  ferry sequence raimi directs the heck  out of the train rescue in which peter  parker unmasked and desperate sticks his  webbing to various passing buildings in  an effort to make a sling with his own  body but what really elevates the scene  above all the rest is the moment in  which peter passes out from sheer  exhaustion and waits to find all the  train passengers staring at him they're  so grateful for his help and so  understanding of how important  spider-man is to their city that they  hand back his mask and promise to never  tell anyone who he is it's a beautiful  final touch to a truly spectacular scene  logan isn't a particularly complex film  by comic book movie standards it doesn't  introduce a horde of new heroes and it  doesn't end with a massive cgi heavy  apocalyptic showdown at its heart this  is a movie about a man who's waiting to  die and finds a reason to live a little  longer considering the heart of the  movie is the relationship between logan  and his young clone laura you'd be  forgiven for expecting some kind of  action team up between the two but this  doesn't occur until the very end of the  movie when it finally does happen  however it's obvious that this is going  to be more than just a fight scene when  laura realizes logan has her back it's a  tremendous emotional payoff and as  logan's body fills up with bullets it  becomes clear that this isn't going to  end like other superhero fights either  the whole sequence is a tremendous  combination of action and emotional  intensity making for a truly memorable  climax and setting up one of the  greatest endings in comic book movie  history thor ragnarok is a film that  sets out to reimagine both thor and the  world around him as a result it's a  movie full of fresh sights and sounds  that offer a lighter and yet more  emotionally resonant take on the god of  thunder there are a number of absolutely  dazzling moments in the film but they  don't get much better than that final  fight as hell as armies close in on his  friends an injured one-eyed thor is  desperate for some kind of help then he  thinks of his father's words realizes  his power comes from within and  unleashes a lightning bolt that finally  slows hella down scored by led  zeppelin's immigrant song thor makes the  mother of all entrances as he joins the  battle on the bifrost throw in valkyrie  and her fireworks strut loki's  redemption and hulk suplexian fenrir and  you've got the recipe for one of the  mcu's best fight scenes spider-man far  from home establishes that the mcu's  peter parker does indeed have a spider  sense which is ant has helpfully  nicknamed the peter tingle he also  apparently has the legendary parker luck  because just when you think the kid has  finally caught a break the film pulls  the rug out from under him by the end of  far from home everything seems to be  going well for peter he's in a  relationship with mj all of his friends  made it home from europe safe and he  cemented his place as tony stark's  successor in the mcu that all comes  crashing down however when it's revealed  by a jay jonah jameson that mysterio has  framed spider-man for his apparent death  and exposes his secret identity to the  world  the long-awaited reintroduction of j  jonah jameson to the mcu was enough to  put jaws on the floor but then the scene  went further by totally ruining peter  parker's life this one's going to take  some fixing a film like captain america  civil war is more or less purpose-built  for big surprise moments and introduced  both black panther and spider-man to the  mcu and pitted various heroes against  each other in a super vs super battle  like no other and that iconic airport  scene's biggest moment turned out to be  the biggest in a very literal sense this  is the moment in which scott lang  reveals that he's capable of growing his  body to a gigantic size seemingly out of  nowhere ant-man grows several dozen feet  and plucks war machine right out of the  air and while he would later reappear in  both ant-man and the wasp and avengers  end game this giant man moment will  always hold a special place in fans  hearts steve rogers isn't a superhero in  the same sense that say thor or the hulk  is nor is he an ordinary man in the same  way that tony stark is steve rogers  treatment with the super soldier serum  has enhanced his body to the point that  he's essentially reached maximum human  potential in terms of strength speed  endurance and more he's quite literally  the best version of a normal human being  without any external enhancements and  because he has a heart determination of  steve rogers he's able to push himself  to the point where even other enhanced  humans wouldn't be able to go  i can do this all day yeah i know  i know  this is perhaps best exemplified in  captain america's civil war when camp  single-handedly holds a helicopter in  place mid takeoff for several seconds  using nothing but a sheer strength and  his willpower even for cap it's quite a  feat and chris evans startling ability  to make his biceps pop is enough to make  this sequence even more memorable  captain marvel arrived in the mcu at a  time when thanos had already snapped  when the avengers had assembled three  times and when characters such as vision  and giant man were practically  commonplace despite all of this captain  marvel had to convince fans that they  were witnessing the creation of the  mcu's most powerful hero someone  stronger than virtually any other  avenger in the room so how did the movie  do this simple by having the hero defeat  a whole army all by herself after  choosing to defend the persecuted  scrolls a fully powered carol danvers  takes out an entire cree squadron and  then flies to a massive creek warship  destroying it in seconds and sending the  surviving bad guys packing and from that  point on there's absolutely no doubt  that carol danvers is a force to be  reckoned with  no one knew quite what to expect from  venom the first solo film to star the  titular anti-hero would it be overly  dark and gritty so self-serious that it  became silly too focused on its creature  to add any real humanity it wasn't easy  to pin down from the marketing either  which is why the end result was so  refreshing a genuinely quirky blend of  darkness action and self-aware humor  venom begins as a sort of body horror  film as eddie brock accidentally comes  across the symbiote and then struggles  to understand why there's a voice in his  head all of a sudden it's an adjustment  period that manifests itself in all  kinds of ways but the most memorable one  occurs when eddie storms into a fancy  san francisco restaurant in an effort to  confront his former partner with his  discoveries of course the venom symbiote  has other plans and by the end of the  scene eddie has submerged himself in a  live lobster tank the whole scene just  gets weirder when eddie snatches up one  of the crustaceans and chows down on a  raw seafood lunch although venom  certainly has splashier moments along  the way this is the one that set the  tone for this particular superhero  franchise funny unpredictable and more  than a little bizarre  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

